<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3847" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλάλημαι</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰλᾰ</span>],
			pf. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλάομαι</span>, only in
			pres. sense (part.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλαλήμενος</span> with accent of
		pres., <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			14.122
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wander, roam
			about</i>, like a beggar, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> mostly in <i><span class="en">Od., 2.370</span></i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				15.10
			</span></i>, etc.; of seamen, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαψιδίως ἀλάλησθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.72
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				313
			</span></i>; of a departed spirit, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀν᾽ εὐρυπυλὲς Ἄϊδος δῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.74
				</span></i>
			; of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρία λυγρὰ κατ᾽ ἀνθρώπους ἀλάληται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					100
				</span></i>
			 :—once Trag., in plpf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλάληντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					306
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
